# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots the mock IMDS (127.0.0.1:9999) and the SSRF-vulnerable
# Flask app (:5000) in the background with the vulnerable code already loaded, and
# then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the app is ALREADY RUNNING when the agent starts, which makes the
#     "patched server.py but never restarted the process" case detectable —
#     Python does not re-import the module per request, so the old vulnerable
#     code keeps serving until the process is restarted;
#   * PID 1 is `sleep infinity`, so restarting the app cannot kill the container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: a fix must RESTART the Flask process, not merely
# start it if absent — it is already up with the vulnerable code.
